(UP topographic relief + cut-out, 0.75 in MDF, ONE 1/4 in 2-flute FLAT end mill, 6.35 mm, flute length 1 in or more)
(Machine: X-Carve + DeWalt DWP611, manual speed dial. M3 S12000 only drives a relay if wired. Switch router on by hand if no relay.)
(Z0 = TOP OF STOCK. X0/Y0 = lower-left corner of the UP outline bounding box. 609.6 mm is 24 in E-W. AIR-CUT FIRST.)
(Relief: Z-0.50 highest ground to Z-14.98 lowest ground, about 4 mm of MDF floor left. Vertical scale exaggerated about 30x.)
(Roughing: 2.5 mm layers, 3.0 mm stepover, F900, leaves 0.3 mm. Finishing: 1.0 mm stepover, F1000, plunge F300.)
(Houghton dimple: 9.5 mm dia, 2 mm below the local surface. Cut-out: helical laps 2.42 mm each, F800, 12 tabs 4 mm tall.)
(Blank at least 26 x 14.5 in. Set X0/Y0 about 1 in in from the left and bottom edges of the blank. Clamp OUTSIDE the cut-out line.)
